    "description": "Cedar Parcel imports weekly shipment manifests from carriers into a staging area before publishing them for warehouse processing. The ImportController reads a CSV file, the ShipmentRow module holds normalized staging records, and a CarrierReference table maps external codes to destination zones and service levels. Every row in the batch must be checked against carrier-code validity, postal-format rules, maximum weight, and duplicate shipment identifiers within the same file. Invalid rows must remain in staging with field-level reasons while valid rows are promoted together into the live Shipment table; publishing must not occur if the batch-level totals or duplicate checks fail. Operators also need a grid showing all rows and their errors. The rules apply to the file and result set as a whole rather than to independently created shipment entities, and no client needs to manipulate a single row outside these operations.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose one component that owns validation and promotion of the entire staged shipment batch as a set operation rather than distributing the rules across request procedures or row-level behaviors.",
    "notes": "table-module primary: set-shaped validation and promotion of a staging batch with tabular grid output; transaction-script is the per-request alternative; service-layer supports as the operation boundary."
  },
